                "reply_count": 10,
                "retweet_count": 3,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Early this morning, after an all/dark of night session, I voted no on the thousand-page reconciliation bill because it cuts taxes for those who least need help at the expense of critical assistance (Medicaid/health, SNAP/food) for those in most need, increases our national debt by $3.8 trillion, reverses sound renewable energy policy, sneaks in a ton of special interest provisions, and more.",
